NOTE on FULL ALL-BASES closure:
  The above used ~200 binding/random bases per (k,gap), not exhaustive.
  For full closure, use ALL C(14,size-1) bases. k=10: 3432, k=11: 3003, k=12: 2002.
  The exhaustive k=10 g=1 check (lrc14_doublet_general_check, 3432 bases) already shows
  the CONSEC base is the worst (not even-AP which fails is_gw for g=1).
  The same should hold for g=2,3,4 by symmetry of the gap structure.
